## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-cloud IaC security policy gates using industry-standard tools (tfsec, Checkov); covers secret management, encryption, versioning, provider pinning, tagging, and backend security.

## Key Concepts
- Secrets in code and tfvars detection
- Cloud storage encryption and versioning
- Provider version pinning and backends
- Tagging and access controls across clouds
- CI integration and local verification for IaC gates

## Code Example
```javascript
// Failing: plaintext secret in Terraform
variable \"db_password\" { default = \"SuperSecret123\" }
resource \"aws_db_instance\" \"db\" {
  password = var.db_password
}

// Passing: secret retrieved from Secrets Manager
data \"aws_secretsmanager_secret_version\" \"db_pass\" {
  secret_id = \"arn:aws:secretsmanager:region:acct:secret:db-password\"
}
resource \"aws_db_instance\" \"db\" {
  password = data.aws_secretsmanager_secret_version.db_pass.secret_string
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you unit-test this gate locally? 
- How would you evolve checks for multi-cloud secret fetch patterns?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical design for tamper-resistant security data collection across heterogeneous Kubernetes estates, addressing post-breach forensics, automation, and resilience.

## Key Concepts

- Tamper-evident logs, audit policy, etcd encryption
- Immutable storage, HMAC signing, key rotation
- Secure log forwarding (webhooks, TLS)
- Runtime security (Falco) and IR playbooks
- Non-repudiation, data retention, failure modes

## Code Example

```javascript
function signEvent(event, key) {
  const crypto = require('crypto');
  const h = crypto.createHmac('sha256', key);
  h.update(event);
  return h.digest('hex');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test integrity guarantees across region failures?
- What are failure modes if the webhook sink is compromised?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to design scalable, privacy-aware audit pipelines for multi-tenant clusters, balancing compliance with operational overhead.

## Key Concepts
- Kubernetes Audit Logs
- Webhook backends & mutating webhooks
- Per-tenant identity normalization
- Privacy redaction & data retention
- Real-time anomaly detection & alerting

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-processor: route audit events to tenant-scoped store
function routeEvent(evt){
  const tenant = evt.user.tenant;
  store.append(tenant, evt);
  if (detectAnomaly(evt, tenant)) alert(tenant, evt);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test for false positives at scale?
- Which storage/processing stack would you choose for 1k+ tenants and why?
